meta {
  type: collection
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

script:pre-request {
  // Every request carries its own identity via an explicit `Cookie` header
  // (see the README). Wipe Bruno's shared cookie jar first so it can't leak a
  // session from a previous request. No-op on builds without `bru.cookies`.
  try { await bru.cookies.clear(); } catch (e) {}
}

docs {
  # Portfolio API - Bruno collection

  Full coverage of the JSON API in `private/api/`, including the authenticated
  `/api/admin/*` surface and every failure mode (401 / 403 / 419 / 422 / 429 /
  404 / 405).

  ## Setup

  1. Run the site:  `php -S localhost:8000 -t public public/router.php`  (+ MySQL).
  2. Seed the test users:  `php bruno/seed-users.php`
     (creates `bruno-admin` / `bruno-user`, password `bruno-dev-pw`).
  3. Select the **Local** environment.
  4. Bruno -> Preferences -> turn the **cookie jar OFF**. Identity is set per
     request through an explicit `Cookie` header; the jar would fight that.
  5. Run the **00 Setup** folder first (or use "Run Collection"). It logs in as
     admin and as a non-admin and stashes `sessionAdmin` / `csrfAdmin` /
     `sessionUser` / `csrfUser` as runtime variables that the rest of the
     collection reads.

  ## Teardown

  `php bruno/seed-users.php --down`

  If any test data lingers:

      DELETE FROM projects WHERE name = 'Bruno Test';
      DELETE FROM opensource_projects WHERE name = 'octocat/Hello-World';
}
